# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for rmw_unix_socket_cpp.
#
# Keep this file as short as it is. Every entry here is a place TSan cannot
# see the synchronisation, NOT a place we have decided to tolerate a race.
#
# The shared-memory discovery registry is a seqlock (registry.cpp). A reader
# copies a slot's payload with plain, unsynchronised loads and then validates
# the copy by re-reading an atomic sequence counter, retrying if the writer
# touched the slot meanwhile. That torn read is the design, not a defect - the
# comment above snapshot_slot says so - but TSan has no seqlock model and
# reports every reader/writer pair it sees.
#
# Only the READER is suppressed. Two threads writing the same slot at once is
# a genuine bug that a seqlock does not permit, and those reports
# (write_slot_payload against teardown_slot) are deliberately left visible.
race:snapshot_slot
